      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Mesenchymal stem/stromal cell based therapies for COVID-19: First iteration of a living systematic review and meta-analysis MSCs and COVID-19",
      "reason": "The title explicitly identifies the report as a \"systematic review and meta-analysis\"."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Mesenchymal stem/stromal cell based therapies for COVID-19: First iteration of a living systematic review and meta-analysis MSCs and COVID-19",
      "reason": "The title identifies the intervention (\"Mesenchymal stem/stromal cell based therapies\") and the population/condition (\"COVID-19\")."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Mesenchymal stem/stromal cell based therapies for COVID-19: First iteration of a living systematic review and meta-analysis MSCs and COVID-19",
      "reason": "The title includes supplementary information indicating it is the \"First iteration of a living systematic review\"."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Mesenchymal stem/stromal cells (MSCs) and their secreted products are a promising therapy for COVID-19 given their immunomodulatory and tissue repair capabilities. Many small studies were launched at the onset of the pandemic",
      "reason": "The authors describe the current state of knowledge regarding MSCs as a therapy for COVID-19 and the context of the pandemic."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Many small studies were launched at the onset of the pandemic, and repeated meta-analysis is critical to obtain timely and sufficient statistical power to determine efficacy.",
      "reason": "The authors explain the need for the review due to the emergence of many small studies and the requirement for sufficient statistical power."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence does not mention the existence of other similar systematic reviews, so this conditional requirement does not apply."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_26",
      "quote": "Thus, the pleiotropic anti-inflammatory and regenerative effects of MSCs may point to several potential mechanisms by which MSCs exert their apparent beneficial effect.",
      "reason": "The authors describe the proposed mechanisms of action for MSCs, including immunomodulation and tissue regeneration."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The intervention (MSC therapy) is a complex intervention, but the manuscript does not include a logic model to show hypothesized relationships between intervention components and outcomes."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 95
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "While the document discusses the study of MSCs for COVID-19, it does not explicitly state the review's objectives or questions using a formal question-formulation framework (e.g., PICO, SPIDER) in the provided text."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "A systematic search of all clinical studies (controlled and uncontrolled) examining the use of MSCs and/or their secretome (which includes conditioned media [MSC-CM] or extracellular vesicles [MSCEVs] derived from MSCs) as a therapeutic intervention was conducted",
      "reason": "The review is of intervention effects (MSCs for COVID-19). The planned comparisons are implicitly stated through the description of the search strategy, which identifies the population (COVID-19 patients, implied by title), intervention (MSCs and/or their secretome), and the comparison (controlled and uncontrolled studies)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "All English-language, full-text, clinical studies examining the use of MSCs or their secretome (MSC-EVs, MSC-CM) as a therapeutic intervention for COVID-19 were included. Studies could be single armed (uncontrolled) or have a comparator or control groups (controlled). ... All symptomatic or asymptomatic patients with con fi rmed SARS-CoV-2 infection ... were included. MSCs derived from any known applicable tissue source ... were acceptable. ... All routes of MSC/secretome administration were acceptable ... MSC-based products could also be administered along with other therapeutic agents ... Studies exclusively investigating other non-MSC-based therapeutics were excluded.",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly defines the inclusion and exclusion criteria regarding the intervention (MSCs/secretome), population (COVID-19 patients), study designs (controlled/uncontrolled), and other relevant characteristics."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "All English-language, full-text, clinical studies ... Studies published in languages other than English, review articles, commentaries, editorials, letters, case reports, conference abstracts, unpublished gray literature and other study types ... were excluded.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies language (English-language), publication status (full-text, excluding gray literature/abstracts), and document type (excluding reviews, commentaries, etc.) as eligibility criteria."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The manuscript does not report excluding studies specifically because outcomes were not measured versus not reported; therefore, this conditional requirement does not apply."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Meta-analysis was performed only when three or more controlled studies reported on the same outcome. Outcomes that were reported in fewer than three controlled studies or for which adequate data for inclusion in meta-analysis was not provided were analyzed in a descriptive manner. ... Potential subgroup analyses were determined a priori in our study protocol with the goal of determining if the effect of MSCs as a therapeutic intervention for COVID-19 was signi fi cantly different for studies that used MSCs from speci fi c tissue sources, MSCs versus secreted factors (MSC-EVs, MSC-CM), or in patients with varying COVID-19 severity.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies how studies were grouped for synthesis (meta-analysis for 3+ controlled studies, descriptive for others) and mentions planned subgroup analyses."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The manuscript does not impose notable restrictions on study eligibility that require a specific rationale beyond standard systematic review criteria."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
}

